#: harwood/tasks/photometry.py:1271
msgid "Every pixel within the radius, less the sky, is a point of intensity against distance from the centre, so that a star is measured by all its pixels and not along a cut. A spline through them is the profile; pixels far from it, a neighbour or a cosmic ray, are taken out and it is fitted again. Too many pieces follow the noise, too few miss the core."
